ill be staged for later approval instead of being published immediately. Staged publishing does not require 2FA, allowing automated workflows to stage packages while deferring proof-of-presence to the approval step. Use `yarn npm stage list`, `yarn npm stage approve`, and `yarn npm stage reject` to manage staged packages.\n\n## Options​\n\nDefinition  | Description\n--- | ---\n\n#### `--access #0`\n\n | The access for the published package (public or restricted)\n\n#### `--tag #0`\n\n | The tag on the registry that the package should be attached to\n\n#### `--tolerate-republish`\n\n | Warn and exit when republishing an already existing version of a package\n\n#### `--otp #0`\n\n | The OTP token to use with the command\n\n#### `--provenance`\n\n | Generate provenance for the pa\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"7465\" /\u003e in subdirectories it will. The `.npmignore` file works just like a `.gitignore`. If there is a `.gitignore` file, and `.npmignore` is missing, `.gitignore`'s contents will be used instead.\n\nCertain files are always included, regardless of settings:\n\n  * `package.json`\n  * `README`\n  * `LICENSE` / `LICENCE`\n  * The file in the \"main\" field\n  * The file(s) in the \"bin\" field\n\n`README` \u0026 `LICENSE` can have any case and extension.\n\nSome files are always ignored by default:\n\n  * `*.orig`\n  * `.*.swp`\n  * `.DS_Store`\n  * `._*`\n  * `.git`\n  * `.hg`\n  * `.lock-wscript`\n  * `.npmrc`\n  * `.svn`\n  * `.wafpickle-N`\n  * `CVS`\n  * `config.gypi`\n  * `node_modules`\n  * `npm-debug.log`\n  * `package-lock.json`\n  * `pnpm-lock.yaml`\n  * `yarn.lock`\n  * `bun.lockb`\n\nMost of these ignored files can be included specifically if included in the `files` globs. Exceptions to this are:\n\n  * `.git`\n  * `.npmrc`\n  * `node_modules`\n  * `package-lock.json`\n  * `pnpm-lock.yaml`\n  * `yarn.lock`\n  * `bun.lockb`\n\nThese cannot be included.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nServer.publish method | Bun module | Bun (https://bun.sh/reference/bun/Server/publish)\nciteturn40search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Modules/Bun/Server/publish\n\nReference\n\nModules/Bun/Server/publish\n\n  * M publish\n\nmethod\n\n# ImageServer.publish\n\npublish(\n\ntopic: string,\n\ndata: string | ArrayBuffer | SharedArrayBuffer | Blob | ArrayBufferView\u003cArrayBufferLike\u003e,\n\ncompress?: boolean\n\n): number;\n\nSend a message to all connected ServerWebSocket clients subscribed to a topic\n\n@param topic\n\nThe topic to publish to\n\n@param data\n\nThe data to send\n\n@param compress\n\nShould the data be compressed? Ignored if the client does not support compression.\n\n@returns\n\n0 if the message was dropped for any subscriber (or there were no subscribers), -1 if backpressure was applied for any subscriber, or the number of bytes sent.\n    \n    `server.publish(\"chat\", \"Hello World\");`\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[85] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk sed -n '420,720p' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_observation.rs \u0026\u0026 rtk sed -n '720,1020p' crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_observation.rs \u0026\u0026 rtk rg -n \\\"ReleaseObservation|ObservationFailure|ExternalConflict|ArtifactUpload|ForgePrepare\\\" crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":40000}); text(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[86] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n\n        .intent()\n        .operations()\n        .iter()\n        .filter_map(|operation| match operation.id() {\n            ReleaseOperationId::RegistryArtifactPublish {\n                package: candidate_package,\n                version: candidate_version,\n                registry: candidate_registry,\n                slot,\n            } if candidate_package == package \u0026\u0026 candidate_version == version \u0026\u0026 candidate_registry == \u0026registry =\u003e {\n                Some(slot.clone())\n            }\n            _ =\u003e None,\n        })\n        .collect::\u003cVec\u003c_\u003e\u003e();\n    let expected_names = expected_slots\n        .iter()\n        .map(|slot| slot.file_name().to_string())\n        .collect::\u003cBTreeSet\u003c_\u003e\u003e();\n    if let Some(file_name) = distributions.keys().find(|name| !expected_names.contains(*name)) {\n        return OperationObservation::Conflict(ExternalConflict::UnexpectedRegistryDistribution {\n            package: package.clone(),\n            version: version.clone(),\n            file_name: file_name.clone(),\n        });\n    }\n\n    let expectations = artifacts.expectations();\n    let mut exact = Vec::new();\n    let mut missing = BTreeSet::new();\n    for slot in expected_slots {\n        let Some(observed) = distributions.get(slot.file_name()) else {\n            missing.insert(MissingWork::RegistryArtifact(slot));\n            continue;\n        };\n        let Some((expected_digest, expected_length)) = expectations.artifact(\u0026slot) else {\n            return OperationObservation::Unverifiable(ObservationFailure::Capability {\n                provider: ObservationProvider::ArtifactCapability,\n            });\n        };\n        if observed.byte_length != expected_length {\n            return OperationObservation::Conflict(ExternalConflict::RegistryLength {\n                slot,\n                observed: observed.byte_length,\n            });\n        }\n        if \u0026observed.digest != expected_digest {\n            return Operat\u003ctruncated omitted_approx_tokens=\"4470\" /\u003e      path.extend(segments.iter().copied());\n    }\n    Some(url.to_string())\n}\n\nfn malformed(provider: ObservationProvider) -\u003e OperationObservation {\n    OperationObservation::Unverifiable(ObservationFailure::MalformedResponse { provider })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use std::{\n        collections::VecDeque,\n        path::Path,\n        sync::{Arc, Mutex},\n    };\n\n    use callisto_model::{CommandError, CommandRunner};\n\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[derive(Clone, Default)]\n    struct RecordingRunner {\n        calls: Arc\u003cMutex\u003cVec\u003c(String, Vec\u003cString\u003e)\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n        outputs: Arc\u003cMutex\u003cVecDeque\u003cResult\u003cCommandOutput, CommandError\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n    }\n\n    impl CommandRunner for RecordingRunner {\n        fn run(\u0026self, program: \u0026str, args: \u0026[\u0026str], _cwd: \u0026Path) -\u003e Result\u003cCommandOutput, CommandError\u003e {\n            self.calls.lock().unwrap().push((\n                program.to_string(),\n                args.iter().map(|value| value.to_string()).collect(),\n            ));\n            self.outputs.lock().unwrap().pop_front().unwrap()\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn output(exit_code: i32, stdout: \u0026str, stderr: \u0026str) -\u003e Result\u003cCommandOutput, CommandError\u003e {\n        Ok(CommandOutput {\n            exit_code: Some(exit_code),\n            stdout: stdout.to_string(),\n            stderr: stderr.to_string(),\n        })\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn github_parser_accepts_real_nonzero_404_response_without_accepting_bare_error_text() {\n        let response = CommandOutput {\n            exit_code: Some(1),\n            stdout: \"HTTP/2 404 Not Found\\r\\ncontent-type: application/json\\r\\n\\r\\n{\\\"message\\\":\\\"Not Found\\\"}\".into(),\n            stderr: \"gh: Not Found (HTTP 404)\".into(),\n        };\n        assert_eq!(parse_http_response(\u0026response).map(|(status, _)| status), Some(404));\n        let bare = CommandOutput {\n            exit_code: Some(1),\n            stdout: String::new(),\n            stderr: \"gh: Not Found (HTTP 404)\".into(),\n        };\n        assert_eq!(parse_http_response(\u0026bare), None);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[87] tool send_message call: {\"target\":\"/root\",\"message\":\"REDACTED\"}\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[88] tool exec call: const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk rg -n \\\"cargo_publish_argv|npm_publish_argv|pypi_publish_argv|detect_npm_package_manager|run_argv|dispatch_registry|npm_version_is_published|cargo_version_is_published|poll_until_published\\\" crates/callisto-graph/src crates/callisto-graph/tests crates/callisto-cli/src\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/callisto-release-recovery\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":16000}); text(r.output);\n\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\n[89] tool exec result: Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n\n48 matches in 2 files:\n\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:55:/// the durable release executor's own `dispatch_registry` had silently\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:59:pub fn cargo_publish_argv(\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:154:/// [`npm_publish_argv`].\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:167:/// executor's `dispatch_registry` used to hardcode plain `npm publish`\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:170:pub fn detect_npm_package_manager(workspace_root: \u0026Path) -\u003e NpmPackageManager {\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:185:/// already-detected `package_manager` (see [`detect_npm_package_manager`]).\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:198:pub fn npm_publish_argv(\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:287:pub fn pypi_publish_argv(\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:519:fn cargo_publish_argv_uses_manifest_path_and_locked_with_no_registry_for_defa...\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:524:let argv = cargo_publish_argv(dir.path(), Path::new(\".\"), \"demo\", \u0026v(\"1.0.0\")...\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:533:fn cargo_publish_argv_adds_registry_flag_when_non_default() {\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:541:let argv = cargo_publish_argv(dir.path(), Path::new(\".\"), \"demo\", \u0026v(\"2.0.0\")...\ncrates/.../commands/registry_argv.rs:546:fn cargo_publish_argv_rejects_on